<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'I don't know if I'm dreaming': Rebuilding lives after Nepal's devastating floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c8b111fc82969e73d2e86e15b0a6ed4bdd5f634c22b440d7e14103a4ce7786b</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T10:16:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260905-i-dont-know-if-im-dreaming-rebuilding-lives-after-nepal-devastating-floods--411c987116c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260905-i-dont-know-if-im-dreaming-rebuilding-lives-after-nepal-devastating-floods" /><summary type="html">With thousands of people driven from their homes by a massive flash flood that swept entire villages away, FRANCE 24 visits a school in Nepal's remote Rasuwa district that has been converted to a temporary shelter for the dispossessed.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: AfD eyes historic state election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1ea00fc1761d1a72188cdbbb92c2d361ec25bfa2811268d50b1f6ad1bbefdda</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T09:58:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-germany-afd-eyes-historic-state-election-win--ec43bc77d6df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-germany-afd-eyes-historic-state-election-win" /><summary type="html">In Saxony-Anhalt, AfD – Germany's far-right party – is polling at 40% or more of voting intentions, just days ahead of the regional election on 6 September 2026. If the AfD wins an absolute majority of seats, it could soon be in charge here. It would be the first time since 1945 that a far-right party has led a German region.
 
To get there, the party is banking on the promise of a return to "the Germany of old", leaning on East German symbols such as Simson mopeds and retro aesthetics. It is a well-established strategy that draws on a gnawing sense of decline for decades and increasing distrust of traditional parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Temporary education centres help flood-displaced children</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65559286ba8d01fc9d464b40775f0b0bae4985b49b4a887ebfda3e20879258d2</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T09:20:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-nepal-temporary-education-centres-help-flood-displaced-children--a00cbf5bab31.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-nepal-temporary-education-centres-help-flood-displaced-children" /><summary type="html">Children displaced by flash floods in Nepal are attending a temporary education centre in Nuwakot, while aid organisations work to support devastated communities.
 
The UN estimates that $158 million worth of buildings have been damaged, with Nepal warning that reconstruction could cost billions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Monaco rally to edge winless PSG and reclaim top spot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed4d53fa271738c6951bf6d0c66687bfbe2a35a5915e916b9a4e89b1ea395811</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T09:16:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260905-monaco-rally-to-edge-winless-psg-and-reclaim-top-spot--5d5bac2ddff7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260905-monaco-rally-to-edge-winless-psg-and-reclaim-top-spot" /><summary type="html">Monaco made it three wins on the trot and reclaimed the top spot by beating Paris Saint-Germain, who were playing their first home match of the season. Luis Enrique's men have now gone four matches without a win.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Trump sends envoys to Moscow, Kyiv with new plan to 'end war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d026303dd06cd7ddbaed0ee8abac5136f76155b34d6d4a0d90cb6e95ea65026</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T09:15:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-war--4a6b13a71f83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-war" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday he is sending envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner to Moscow and Kyiv with a plan to end more than four years of war in Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two senior Reform UK officials resign as Farage faces fresh foreign donations scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f322c3e54bd214fe94bee6fa794e64e84a1df6871071a7466cebbf598e1475d</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:30:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-two-senior-reform-uk-officials-resign-as-farage-faces-fresh-foreign-donations-scandal--c43eb44d3d6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-two-senior-reform-uk-officials-resign-as-farage-faces-fresh-foreign-donations-scandal" /><summary type="html">Two senior officials from the hard-right Reform UK party stepped down Friday following a hidden-camera investigation that appeared to show them soliciting substantial foreign funding for party-commissioned opinion polls and a potential £500,000 donation from a US donor – banned under UK law.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Explosions of unknown origin heard near Iran's Kharg Island</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc5b264a272eb355dd24008c2df8d5aedad05d3bf206696936083f4c31b3a4b4</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T05:01:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-middle-east-live-israeli-strikes-on-south-and-east-lebanon-kill-three-people--9a0ff2430b05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-middle-east-live-israeli-strikes-on-south-and-east-lebanon-kill-three-people" /><summary type="html">A correspondent for the semi-official Fars news agency on Saturday reported hearing explosions of unknown origin near Iran's Kharg Island in ‌the Gulf, ⁠a key oil terminal. The state-affiliated Nournews said there were unconfirmed reports ‌from local sources that an Iranian tanker ‌had been targeted by a missile fired by US forces. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump sends envoys to Moscow and Kyiv with new plan to 'end the war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a51393a642968f29d93b29285b85f4f7b959feeecb44a71ff6d3a165a13e40f9</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T02:37:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-and-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-the-war--2b81279000c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-and-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-the-war" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are travelling to Moscow and Kyiv this weekend with what US President Donald Trump says is a new proposal to end the war in Ukraine. Despite Trump's promises to resolve the conflict, Washington's efforts to broker a peace have so far come to nothing.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Uber withdraws from Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b67222f9bd508fe35c180af4f6bca78b60ce032195d65b11aae35aa8251052d6</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T20:39:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uber-withdraws-from-nigeria--7fddf4430022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uber-withdraws-from-nigeria" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, a UN report says foreign fighters and support networks are fuelling Sudan’s war and worsening violence against civilians. Also, Uber is pulling out of Nigeria and Uganda, leaving thousands of drivers scrambling for new sources of income. And finally, we discuss the festival with co-director Diarah N’Daw-Spech and Laurence Cole, co-producer of the Nigerian film "Shadow of Greed".</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>‘Major potential breaches of British election law’: Inside Channel 4’s investigation into Reform UK</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c548cb09fa4d579be84371d503767a0f0b33d621fc0eb6f8b74898c8fa94add5</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:52:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-major-potential-breaches-of-british-election-law-understanding-channel-4-s-investigation--100a26e41120.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-major-potential-breaches-of-british-election-law-understanding-channel-4-s-investigation" /><summary type="html">Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Peter Geoghegan, an award-winning investigative journalist. He's the editor of the Substack Democracy for Sale and the author of the best-selling book "Democracy for Sale". Geoghegan explains the significance of the Channel 4 investigation not simply over the conduct allegedly captured on camera, but in the broader question of how political influence is financed and made visible, or invisible, within British democracy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>German power grid sabotage attack linked to ‘climate extremism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d1d43083aaef8ec3800b3f2f38667fcb4232d0906a3c49b57310fd7a5a8c4a2</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:40:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism--b5a9f0391572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism" /><summary type="html">German Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt on Friday said the evidence in a recent spate of sabotage attacks on power grids across the country points to a militant climate activist.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UN ditches Mercator map to adopt more accurate one reflecting Africa's true size</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c276ec41e9651798e930d2603407214745c917201b2dcb74b124d674e9f8395b</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:31:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/earth/20260904-un-ditches-mercator-map-to-adopt-more-accurate-one-reflecting-africa-s-true-size--2bb05ca3b5d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/earth/20260904-un-ditches-mercator-map-to-adopt-more-accurate-one-reflecting-africa-s-true-size" /><summary type="html">The UN General Assembly on Friday voted to shift away from the 16th-century Mercator map, designed by Flemish cartographer Gerardus Mercator, for a more accurate one reflecting the true size of continents. The resolution, spearheaded by several African countries and co-sponsored by France, was backed by 164 countries. The US voted against and six other states abstained.</summary><category term="Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s ‘Most Dangerous Man’: PR gift for the AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7b054b7361ca76acceb0a9a4e50290118165cc317568aa1d267bfccc159f481</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:31:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd--f852f5df9336.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd" /><summary type="html">The Ukrainian capital was hit by Russia’s most intense wave of air attacks on Kyiv, reportedly in four years, with Reuters describing air raid sirens, drones, cruise and ballistic missiles exhausting Ukraine’s defence system, with 12 people killed and the Ukrainian foreign minister making a direct appeal to Western allies for more Patriot interceptor missiles.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's West Bank camp displacements could be crime against humanity, UN says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3813d55ba0601863bec275291dbfa6486a4c385125420d199039d87acf8be497</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T16:26:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says--03f625c09b2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says" /><summary type="html">The Israeli government's forced displacement of the entire populations of three West Bank refugee camps in January 2025 could amount to crimes against humanity, a UN report warned Friday. More than 33,000 Palestinians forced out of the Jenin, Nur Shams and Tulkarm camps have not been permitted to return home. Israel slammed the report for "spreading misinformation".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms start with North Carolina distributing mail-voting ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5c9432014534f64531fd113cdd23c721ab0a88c17325886a50dbe9b79bf263a</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:53:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-us-midterms-begin-with-chaos-over-mail-voting-crackdown--b948c78e1c61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-us-midterms-begin-with-chaos-over-mail-voting-crackdown" /><summary type="html">North Carolina on Friday became the first state authorised to begin sending out ballots, formally launching the 2026 US midterms as President Donald Trump’s administration fights to impose sweeping restrictions on the practice.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Italian opposition fragmented: No alternative leader, no other possible leader than Giorgia Meloni'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e5e2537095f9d05ded4fbf0fe16e67695c515b65f488bb131fd891186b2627d</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-m--1c36e6864261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-meloni-1" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Political analyst Lorenzo Pregliasco, co-founder of polling agency YouTrend and adjunct professor at the University of Bologna. He argues that Giorgia Meloni’s unusual longevity in office is best understood not simply as a record of political strength, but as the product of a carefully calibrated governing strategy. Meloni has maintained stability partly by avoiding structural reforms disruptive enough to mobilize multiple constituencies against her at once. Her dominance within Fratelli d’Italia, the absence of a credible alternative leader, and a fragmented opposition have reinforced that advantage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider, the ideologist behind the AFD’s plans in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c55f3af4c110108fedd6a856a96c603fa6742ec79f3340cf1eddaf9ee64dbba2</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:34:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt--220beb71b19c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt" /><summary type="html">The far-right German political party Alternative for Germany could win a historical victory in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt in key elections this Sunday. The party’s agenda is more radical than ever and inspired by the proposals of an influential ideologist in the region: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump envoys Witkoff, Kushner to visit Russia and Ukraine in coming days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd2600a6440d67938a3e7b144d230df6f90920623291105c235a0309206c7a91</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:29:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-envoys-witkoff-kushner-to-visit-russia-and-ukraine-in-coming-days--2d9b95db2738.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-envoys-witkoff-kushner-to-visit-russia-and-ukraine-in-coming-days" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are expected to arrive in Kyiv for a first-time visit on Sunday, several sources reported. Witkoff and Kushner – Trump's son-in-law – have been involved in shuttle diplomacy between Russia and Ukraine, travelling to Moscow multiple times, and are expected to visit Kyiv this weekend. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>On the ground: Russian drone strikes Ukraine security service headquarters in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:762029199a971897f2cc15e289b3f9a3cdf6d58c10f28caf8c0b365d1fc2ea10</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:24:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-on-the-ground-russian-drone-strikes-ukraine-security-service-headquarters-in-kyiv--af0328695810.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-on-the-ground-russian-drone-strikes-ukraine-security-service-headquarters-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone struck the headquarters of Ukraine's SBU security services on Friday, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said, accusing Moscow of aiming directly at the SBU head's personal office. Zelensky said he had instructed the SBU to deliver an "appropriate, tangible response" to the strike, while Ukraine's Foreign Minister Andriy Sybiga described it as a "major escalation". FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports from Kyiv, Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>US judge declares mistrial in Lindsay Clancy child-killing case after jury deadlock</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16968be897579567b68a1d183da67ea7c2a0e4b18e26fd834eacafaf5b00e51b</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:21:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-judge-declares-mistrial-in-case-of-us-woman-who-killed-her-children--609fadb47579.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-judge-declares-mistrial-in-case-of-us-woman-who-killed-her-children" /><summary type="html">A judge in Massachusetts on Friday declared a mistrial in the Lindsay Clancy murder court case after jurors were unable to reach a unanimous verdict on her criminal responsibility for killing her three young children. The case sparked a public debate over maternal mental health.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ethan Hawke leads the charge at Deauville's 52nd American Film Festival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:857d386c98d7bb5f646ede4c15c2ca6915f3e61be674e9baa5fb1b3d0a34e811</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:19:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260904-ethan-hawke-leads-the-charge-at-deauville-s-52nd-american-film-festival--98a681434fde.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260904-ethan-hawke-leads-the-charge-at-deauville-s-52nd-american-film-festival" /><summary type="html">The Normandy coast has become Hollywood-sur-mer once again, as the annual film festival welcomes talent from the United States. FRANCE 24's Genie Godula takes time out from hosting the opening ceremony in Deauville to bring us an overview of the features screening there.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>France announces €1 billion aid for farmers after climate-hit summer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d8989f9dbcf9cb1032b381260cf7c8f10c562923f00db26daae9e857fdec066</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:12:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-_1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer--e6ed56d5d705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-%E2%82%AC1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer" /><summary type="html">France has recorded its hottest summer on record this year as the country battled heatwaves, drought and massive wildfires. The extreme weather has continued into September, with France's national weather service placing five departments on orange alert for several days. Temperatures are expected to reach 40°C in some areas. France's agriculture minister also announced a plan to unlock over 1 billion euros in aid to the agriculture sector, which has been severely affected by the extreme weather.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Russian drone ‘aimed directly’ at Ukraine security service HQ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c677778e7d1b91f4fbfcb1481ef70218593f3049637572c6ce6c7d1e8640d7b8</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:07:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says--9847636126d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says" /></entry></feed>
